        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · Europe</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Vienna (1683)</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">12 September 1683, the last day of a siege that began on 14 July 1683</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">Kahlenberg and the ground north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>, then the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> capital, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> under King John III <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-iii-sobieski">Sobieski</a>, with Ernst Rüdiger von Starhemberg commanding the garrison; the relief army is put at 65,000 soldiers with 165–200 guns by one assessment, and at 70,000–80,000 by another. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-vizier">Grand Vizier</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kara-mustafa-pasha">Kara Mustafa Pasha</a>, with an army given as 28,400 to 50,000 in the battle</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The relief army defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> was saved. The Ottomans fought on until 1699 and lost control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a>.</span></div>
        </div>
