    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The siege lasted two months, from 14 July to 12 September 1683, and the relief army and the garrison together defeated the Ottoman army in a single day.</li><li>Strengths are disputed: the Ottoman army in the battle is given as 28,400 to 50,000 men, and the relief army as 65,000 or as 70,000–80,000.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> fought on until 1699, when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-karlowitz">Treaty of Karlowitz</a> ceded much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Before the siege the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> had been at peace for 20 years under the Peace of Vasvár, and the allied cavalry charge on 12 September has been called the largest known cavalry charge in history.</p></aside>
    </section>

